<title>JAPAN: New South Wales launches 4.8% dual samurai--Nomura.</title>
<headline>New South Wales launches 4.8% dual samurai--Nomura.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/Australian dollar dual currency samurai bond issue was announced by lead-manager Nomura Securities on Thursday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  New South Wales Treasury Corp</p>
<p> AMT		 30 billion yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    4.8 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  22 Jan 1999</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  22 Jan 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	Jan 13 to Jan 21</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AA, Moody's Aa2</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Nomura Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Fuji Bank</p>
<p>NOTE: Holders of the samurai bonds will receive A$5,521.81 for each 500,000-yen bond held at maturity.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
</text>
